1. RECAP (DAY 27)
-----------------
completions, parallelism, backoffLimit, activeDeadlineSeconds,
ttlSecondsAfterFinished, restartPolicy Never/OnFailure, CronJobs.


2. INDEXED JOBS AND PER-INDEX RETRIES
-------------------------------------
completionMode: Indexed gives each pod JOB_COMPLETION_INDEX.
Real uses: process file shard N, render frame N, train fold N.

  backoffLimitPerIndex: 2     each index retried up to 2 times
  maxFailedIndexes: 3         give up when more than 3 indexes failed
One bad shard no longer burns the whole Job's retry budget.
status.failedIndexes / completedIndexes show exactly which failed.


3. POD FAILURE POLICY
---------------------
Decide what a failure MEANS:
  podFailurePolicy:
    rules:
    - action: FailJob            # a real bug: stop immediately
      onExitCodes:
        containerName: worker
        operator: In
        values: [42]
    - action: Ignore             # node was drained/preempted: not
      onPodConditions:           # the app's fault, don't count it
      - type: DisruptionTarget
Actions: FailJob, Ignore, Count (default), FailIndex.
Requires restartPolicy: Never.


4. SUCCESS POLICY
-----------------
successPolicy (newer): mark an Indexed Job successful when certain
indexes succeed (e.g. "index 0 is the leader; when it finishes, done").


5. SUSPEND AND QUEUEING
-----------------------
  spec.suspend: true    create the Job without starting pods; set to
                        false to start. Batch queue systems (Kueue)
                        use this to admit jobs when quota allows.


6. WORK-QUEUE PATTERN
---------------------
Fixed completions are awkward when work arrives continuously. Instead:
  producer pushes tasks to a queue (Redis list, RabbitMQ, SQS, Kafka)
  N worker pods pop tasks until the queue is empty (Job) or forever
  (Deployment), and an autoscaler sizes N by queue length (Day 58).
Workers must be idempotent and acknowledge only after success.


7. CLEANUP
----------
  ttlSecondsAfterFinished on every Job (or the cluster fills with
  completed pods); CronJob history limits; owner references so
  deleting a parent removes children.


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- Indexed + backoffLimitPerIndex for sharded work.
- podFailurePolicy separates app bugs from infrastructure noise.
- suspend lets a queue system decide when Jobs run.
- Work queues + autoscaling for continuous background work.
